# Plans and limits

Every plan includes tracing, the cost view, and the trace viewer. Higher plans add more volume, longer history, and extra features.

| | Free | Pro | Team |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Spans per month | 10,000 | 500,000 | 2,000,000 |
| Spans per day | 2,000 | No daily cap | No daily cap |
| Projects | 2 per account | 3 | Unlimited |
| Members | 1 | 5 | 20 |
| History | 7 days | 30 days | 90 days |
| Requests per minute (per project) | 300 | Plan default | Plan default |
| Alerts (email and Slack) | Not included | Included | Included |
| Ask AI | Ready-made questions | Any question | Any question |

## What happens at a limit

When a Free project reaches its monthly or daily span limit, Uncoil stops saving new data until the limit resets. Data that is already saved stays. Monthly counts reset at the start of each UTC month, and daily counts reset at midnight UTC.

The refused request gets a `429` response. The body names the limit (`plan_limit_reached` or `daily_limit_reached`), says when to retry, and includes an `upgradeUrl` that points to the plans.

Pro and Team projects get a 10% buffer above the included spans before new data is refused. You are never billed extra for going over.

Very large spans on the Free plan are shortened instead of refused, so a long prompt still appears in the trace, just trimmed.

## Before you reach the limit

The dashboard shows a notice when a project has used 80% of its monthly spans. A Free project owner also gets one email at 80% and one when the project reaches its monthly limit and new data is paused, each at most once a month, so the limit never comes as a surprise.

## Alerts, Ask AI, and history

- **Alerts.** Creating alert rules is part of Pro and Team. Rules that already exist on a Free project keep running.
- **Ask AI.** On Free, the four ready-made questions in the trace viewer work as usual. Typing your own question needs Pro or Team.
- **History.** Date ranges longer than the plan's history are not available. Free shows up to 7 days.

See the [pricing page](https://www.uncoil.dev/pricing) for current prices.
